@startuml
title AWS Cost Dashboard – Complete End-to-End Process

actor User
participant "Frontend (Next.js)" as Frontend
participant "Laravel API" as API
participant "Auth Logic" as Auth
participant "CostReportController" as ReportCtrl
participant "CostByService" as ServiceCtrl
participant "CsvParser" as Parser
participant "CsvReportToData" as DataOps
database PostgreSQL as DB

== 1. Authentication ==
User -> Frontend : Login (Email/Password)
Frontend -> API : POST /api/login
API -> Auth : Validate Credentials
Auth -> DB : Check User & Hash
DB --> Auth : User Query Result
alt Valid Credentials
    Auth --> API : Generate Sanctum Token
    API --> Frontend : Return Access Token
    Frontend -> Frontend : Store Token & Redirect to Dashboard
else Invalid Credentials
    API --> Frontend : 401 Unauthorized
    Frontend --> User : Show Error Message
end

== 2. Data Ingestion (Manual Upload Flow) ==
note right of User
  Alternative: S3 Webhook (Automated)
  See s3_webhook.puml for details
end note

User -> Frontend : Upload Cost Report (CSV)
Frontend -> API : POST /api/aws/cost-report/upload
API -> ReportCtrl : uploadReport(Request)
ReportCtrl -> Parser : parse(fileContent)
Parser --> ReportCtrl : parsed data (mapped columns)

ReportCtrl -> DataOps : processData(parsedData)
DataOps -> DataOps : Aggregate & Format Dates
DataOps --> ReportCtrl : processed records

ReportCtrl -> DataOps : saveToDatabase()
DataOps -> DB : INSERT cost_uploads
DataOps -> DB : BATCH INSERT cost_records
DB --> DataOps : Success
DataOps --> ReportCtrl : Upload Summary
ReportCtrl --> Frontend : 200 OK (Upload Complete)
Frontend --> User : Show Success Notification

== 3. Dashboard Visualization (Parallel Data Fetching) ==
User -> Frontend : Load Dashboard (/home)

par Fetch Monthly Trend
    Frontend -> API : GET /aws/cost-report/monthly-trend
    API -> ReportCtrl : monthlyTrend()
    ReportCtrl -> DB : Query (Group by Month)
    DB --> ReportCtrl : Trend Data
    ReportCtrl --> Frontend : JSON Response
end

par Fetch Account Breakdown
    Frontend -> API : GET /aws/cost-report/account-breakdown
    API -> "CostBreakdown" as BreakCtrl : accountBreakdown()
    BreakCtrl -> DB : Query (Group by Account)
    DB --> BreakCtrl : Account Data
    BreakCtrl --> Frontend : JSON Response
end

par Fetch Service Costs
    Frontend -> API : GET /cost/services/by-account
    API -> ServiceCtrl : serviceByAccount()
    ServiceCtrl -> DB : Query (Group by Service)
    DB --> ServiceCtrl : Service Data
    ServiceCtrl --> Frontend : JSON Response
end

Frontend -> Frontend : Render Charts (Recharts)
Frontend --> User : Display Interactive Dashboard

== 4. Detailed Analysis (Filtering) ==
User -> Frontend : View Service Analysis Page
Frontend -> API : GET /cost/services/months
API -> ServiceCtrl : availableMonths()
ServiceCtrl -> DB : DISTINCT month_year
DB --> ServiceCtrl : List of Months
ServiceCtrl --> Frontend : Months List

User -> Frontend : Select Month & Account Filter
Frontend -> API : GET /cost/services/account/{account}?month_year=...
API -> ServiceCtrl : servicesByAccount(Request, Account)
ServiceCtrl -> DB : Query with WHERE clauses
DB --> ServiceCtrl : Filtered Service Data
ServiceCtrl --> Frontend : Updated Data
Frontend --> User : Update Grid & Charts

@enduml
